cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Causalista, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Causalista: a small, local model that decides what to adjust for, and says when the data cannot answer"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-24
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/coppead/causalista"
url: "https://huggingface.co/coppead/causalista-4b"
authors:
  - family-names: Fonseca
    given-names: André
    affiliation: "COPPEAD Graduate School of Business, Federal University of Rio de Janeiro (UFRJ)"
keywords:
  - causal inference
  - adjustment set
  - abstention
  - synthetic data
  - reinforcement learning with verifiable rewards
  - small language models
  - management
abstract: >-
  Causalista 0.1 is a 4B-parameter model, fine-tuned from Qwen3-4B, for one decision in
  causal analysis: given a table's column dictionary and a story of how the data were
  generated, which columns to adjust for to measure the effect of an intervention, or
  whether the effect is not identifiable with these columns. It was trained on synthetic
  worlds with a known answer, scored by a verifier that knows the true causal graph, and
  measured on held-out worlds in three languages and on cases that simulate text written
  by people. Model, GGUF files and dataset are published under the coppead organisation
  on the Hugging Face Hub; the generator, verifier, estimator and evaluation harness are
  in this repository. The project was built by the author with an AI coding assistant; the model
  and dataset cards record who wrote what.
